.TH BINGUX-CALENDAR 1 "2026-11-09" "Bingux 0.1.0" "Bingux"
.SH NAME
bingux-calendar \- calendar for the Bingux desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bingux-calendar
.RB [ \-\-reminders ]
.RI [ FILE.ics | YYYY-MM-DD | today ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bingux-calendar
opens the Calendar window with day, week, month, year and agenda views, repeating
events, quick add and reminders.
Events are kept in ordinary calendar files, one folder for each calendar, so no
account is needed.
.PP
Only one Calendar window runs.
A second launch hands its argument to the running window, which comes to the
front.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I FILE.ics
A calendar file. Calendar offers to import its events.
.TP
.I YYYY-MM-DD
Shows that day.
.TP
.B today
Shows today.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-reminders
Runs with no window and shows reminders as they come due.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/bingux-calendar/calendars/ID/
One folder for each calendar: its events as
.I .ics
files, its name in
.IR displayname ,
and its colour in
.IR color .
Another program that writes the same layout (for example vdirsyncer) is read
as it changes.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bingux-calendar/settings.json
The view, the first day of the week, the time format, the calendar new events
go in and the calendars that are hidden.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bingux\-settings (1),
.BR xdg\-open (1)
.PP
Documentation: docs/calendar-app.md in the Bingux source.
.SH AUTHORS
Kieran Drewett and the Bingux contributors.
